{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026","id":1395019,"title":"Min maxing \u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T23:41:10-07:00","id":1395019,"title":"Min maxing \u2026","content":"If I have holographic projection 3 and the expand deviation And a 5 scar power I could create A dump truck Size 25, Durability 1, with 26 structure. If you were storyteller Would you allow me to create A size 1 knife With 26 structure Would it have to be A size 25 knife with one durability. I'm hoping to create resilient small things. Too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T03:30:25-07:00","id":1395050,"title":"","content":"I don't have the Deviant book, so I don't know the specifics of the powers in question, but if a size 1 knife were to have 26 structure, that would mean 25 durability. That means only direct aggravated damage or attacks dealing at least 26 damage could damage the knife. There are few things I've seen in any game as broken as that possibility, so I would never allow this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:01:23-07:00","id":1395055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026#post1395019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were storyteller Would you allow me to create A size 1 knife With 26 structure</div> </div> </div> </div> No, the text is very clear: the Durability of an illusion is always 1.<br /> <br /> I think it would be fine as a custom Deviation, though perhaps not to that extent. Something like...<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Density (+1 Magnitude):</b> When creating a hologram smaller than Size 5, the Remade can increase its Durability by up to (5 - Size). This Deviation can\u2019t modify the Magnitude <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf</span></span> or <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf</span></span> versions of Holographic Projection.</div> A Size 1 knife could then have a Durability of 6 and a Structure of 7, rendering it basically indestructible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:23:20-07:00","id":1395060,"title":"","content":"Given how utterly rarely people trying to break items as minor as knives.... I'm not really sure why an unbreakable-by-mundane-means knife is at all broken. It's not like it does more damage. It's not like it stops someone from chopping your arm off making the knife useless to you.<br /> <br /> While a starting level mage isn't going to pump out a knife as resilient as the OP's post (mostly because Alter Integrity makes you split your Potency between Durability and Structure rather than increased Durability increasing Structure), they could still make a lasting Durability 11/Structure 12 knife, or a Durability 15/Structure 4 knife (or any number of combinations) easily enough.<br /> <br /> There's a point where bigger and bigger numbers really just don't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T10:16:01-07:00","id":1395100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395060#post1395060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how utterly rarely people trying to break items as minor as knives.... I'm not really sure why an unbreakable-by-mundane-means knife is at all broken. It's not like it does more damage. It's not like it stops someone from chopping your arm off making the knife useless to you</div> </div> </div> </div>The brokenness of the Durability 25 knife isn't in the knife specifically, but that it implies any Size 1 object could have that Durability rating. Having an effectively unbreakable Size 1 object of your choosing available is not something I as ST would ever want to deal with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T14:20:37-07:00","id":1395150,"title":"","content":"OK but... why? You're saying this like Durability is some insanely powerful trait.<br /> <br /> Actually, let's skip the mechanical details for a moment:<br /> <br /> What would be broken about a power that lets you make a Size 1 object unbreakable without supernatural powers for a scene? Some other unit of time that you feel gets to a specific issue?<br /> <br /> What, in your experience as a ST with this system, says this is something that players should not have access to?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T02:54:28-07:00","id":1395277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395150#post1395150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, in your experience as a ST with this system, says this is something that players should not have access to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, as both player and ST, I've seen abuse of power being used too often. It's the &quot;give an inch, they'll take a yard&quot; problem that I just don't enjoy in games. <br /> <br /> Additionally, the way I understood what was being described was as though Size and Durability simply needed to sum to 26 to be a valid object. 21 Durability is still effectively unbreakable. I'm not sure if these powers also have rules for acting as armour, but high durability suggests to me a high armour rating. I may be very incorrect about that, but it seems to me like a very safe assumption","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T03:23:35-07:00","id":1395285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395277#post1395277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, as both player and ST, I've seen abuse of power being used too often. It's the &quot;give an inch, they'll take a yard&quot; problem that I just don't enjoy in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a player problem, not a system problem. As an ST I would either tell them to cut it out (or just roll with it if that's the kind of game they want to play as long as it doesn't break the fun for the other players).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395277#post1395277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, the way I understood what was being described was as though Size and Durability simply needed to sum to 26 to be a valid object. 21 Durability is still effectively unbreakable. I'm not sure if these powers also have rules for acting as armour, but high durability suggests to me a high armour rating. I may be very incorrect about that, but it seems to me like a very safe assumption</div> </div> </div> </div>As already mentioned, Durability is set to 1 so it's not a problem, and even if it were you could not possibly use it as either armour or concealment because of the low Size. Not even if you have five of them (which is the maximum amount) would you be able to combine them into anything except the smallest piece of armour that would provide no protection unless the enemy actively aimed at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:36:49-07:00","id":1395377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395277#post1395277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, as both player and ST, I've seen abuse of power being used too often. It's the &quot;give an inch, they'll take a yard&quot; problem that I just don't enjoy in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument might have merit if we were talking about the improvised weapon rules and a player deciding to make a not-weapon to attack someone with because improvised weapons base their damage on Durability. But that's the sort of metagaming logic that Tessie rightfully points out is a player problem: &quot;My character uses a power to create a high Durability heavy box instead of a baseball bat to use a weapon so the damage is based off the improvised weapon rules instead,&quot; is something you call BS on and rule against, because that's not what a character would actually think; while a character could still very reasonably want to use their powers to have a massive Durability rating on a wall they're using as Cover while being shot at... because that's totally a legit choice for them to make and increasing Durability is a valid option there.<br /> <br /> You're also dodging the question: Why would a power that lets you make an unbreakable (unless broken with other powers) a problem? That needs to be addressed before any sort of honing in on whether or not you can make a nigh invincible item through really high Durability as being a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if these powers also have rules for acting as armour, but high durability suggests to me a high armour rating. I may be very incorrect about that, but it seems to me like a very safe assumption </div> </div> </div>This is a very poor assumption. Armor and shields have ratings that are independent of their Durability. This makes a lot of sense when you consider something like a Kevlar vest, which you can cut up with a decent pair of shears, still being able to offer significant protection from a bullet. The is a tendency for &quot;hard&quot; armors, like steel plate mail or a military combat vehicle, to have high Durability, but there is not direct mathematical correlation between them.<br /> <br /> Going back to Mage for a bit, it's notable that the spell to increase a piece of armor's ratings is a completely different spell from changing it's Durability or Structure. Giving a t-shirt Durability 10 doesn't give it any armor rating (a bullet just shoves the fabric into your PC's body as it puts a hole in you instead of actually slowing it down to prevent damage). Giving a t-shirt a 3/3 armor rating doesn't change it's Durability or Structure.<br /> <br /> As previously indicated, the big situation where Durability is going to come into play defensively in combat, is as Cover. Cover can be circumvented very easily: move to a different angle where you can attack with either concealment penalties or not penalties at all. Cover has to completely impose itself between an attacker and the target to force the attacker to penetrate the Cover's Durability in hopes of harming the target.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:24:01-07:00","id":1395401,"title":"","content":"In my first (and current!) DtD game, I have a player who is a bit of a min/maxer. He designed everything in his character so he could max at whatever he wanted.<ul><li>Skills? Fungible Knowledge to move his 5 dot skill to any area when needed.</li> <li>Forms? Mutable Form so that he could have any Form ability he wanted <i>and</i> Terrible Form to have more Form abilities <i>and</i> a Merit to make it easier to activate Form abilities.</li> <li>Merits? &quot;Allies into Gold&quot; to move Contacts and Resources around, maxing out when needed.</li> </ul>This is my own fault as ST to not have caught this and I have had a discussion with the player to rein in some abuse. I am more used to point-buy systems where the cost of this flexibility was a significant portion of the character's total points. <br /> <br /> Efficient character design is fine but I draw the line when it becomes impossible for all of the other players to participate in the story because they chose a different build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:59:00-07:00","id":1395412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395401#post1395401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skills? Fungible Knowledge to move his 5 dot skill to any area when needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only works as long as he hasn't used both Skills and using it more times in one day than his Resolve triggers a compromise roll. What's the five-dot Skill he's trading off?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forms? Mutable Form so that he could have any Form ability he wanted <i>and</i> Terrible Form to have more Form abilities <i>and</i> a Merit to make it easier to activate Form abilities. </div> </div> </div>Amorphous only works in full demonic form and costs Aether for every switch \u2014 it's a Process that functionally applies the same costs as partial transformation to your regular demonic form. Versatile Transformation only helps with partial transformation and Terrible Form doesn't help with the fact that a compromise roll is being made whenever he opens up form abilities for use.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Merits? &quot;Allies into Gold&quot; to move Contacts and Resources around, maxing out when needed. </div> </div> </div>It's an Exploit. He's either bleeding Willpower or risking compromise every time he uses it. This specific Exploit also applies an explicit scaled penalty to the attendant compromise roll and takes an hour per roll to use, and it's specifically related to Merits that demons have to either access through attached Covers or risk compromise by looping people in on the fact that they're demons.<br /> <br /> Like, he's clearly invested resources in being a Swiss Army knife, but the build you're describing is going to draw attention from exercising that versatility too frequently compared to other characters' having more consistent fields of specialty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T06:57:18-07:00","id":1395832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1395019-min-maxing-\u2026?p=1395377#post1395377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As previously indicated, the big situation where Durability is going to come into play defensively in combat, is as Cover. Cover can be circumvented very easily: move to a different angle where you can attack with either concealment penalties or not penalties at all. Cover has to completely impose itself between an attacker and the target to force the attacker to penetrate the Cover's Durability in hopes of harming the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Berserker style's Manic Brutality, making the weapon's durability it's damage. Hello 26 damage knife.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T09:24:41-07:00","id":1395851,"title":"","content":"Except, as noted, that isn't how Deviant's rules work, and Durability enhancing powers rarely go that high.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, a power that directly increases weapon Damage is going to perform better than using a power to get a high Durability item, and buying up a Merit just to use Durability for damage and that damages the item in the process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}